course: dictionary
lesson: 9638
title: Stun: dizzy, shocked or amazing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word stun is a verb with two main meanings. It can mean to hit a person or animal so they are dizzy or knocked out for a short time. It can also mean to shock someone so much that they cannot think or speak for a moment.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is which. «A bird stunned by hitting a window» tells you the bird was knocked dizzy for a while. «Stunned silence» in a story tells you that everyone went quiet because they were shocked.
explain: Stunning, as an adjective, means extremely beautiful or impressive. Try the meaning in the sentence: «a stunning view» is a view so lovely you cannot stop looking at it. If your meaning still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Stun means to knock someone dizzy, or to shock them so they cannot speak for a moment.
fact: Stunned is the past form, as in «She was stunned by the news».
fact: Stuns and stunning are other forms; stunning can also be an adjective meaning amazing.
fact: Some animals use stunning to catch food: «Electric eels use strong shocks to stun prey and scare enemies».
fact: «Absolutely stunning» means really, really amazing, and a «stun gun» is a tool that stuns.
exercise: «The pistol shrimp's bubble bursts with a loud crack that stuns small fish.» What does stuns mean here? | Gives them a warm bath | Makes them grow bigger | *Shocks them so they are dazed for a moment | Lets them swim away fast
exercise: «Her stunning painting won first prize.» What does stunning mean here? | Very small and hard to see | Very noisy and loud | *Extremely beautiful or impressive | Dark and gloomy
exercise: Find the word that means shocked so much you cannot speak for a moment. | stub | stung | *stunned | stern
test: «Electric rays can stun fish with shocks of up to about 200 volts.» What does stun mean here? | Make hungry | *Make dizzy or knock out for a short time | Wash clean | Make a loud noise
test: Ella says, «The news was stunning.» Which meaning fits best? | *Amazing or shocking | Cold and wet | Boring and slow | Quiet and calm
exam: Which two meanings does stun have as a verb? | Walk or run very fast | *Hit or shock someone so they are dizzy, or shock them so they cannot speak | Sing a quiet song | Cook and eat food
